# SYNTHETIC. Written from RFC 5804 (ManageSieve), with capability lines in the shape a
# Pigeonhole server sends them. Not a recording.
# Bytes that arrive in plaintext after the server's OK to STARTTLS, before the
# handshake, would otherwise be read as the TLS session's capabilities. Here they
# arrive in the same read as the OK and advertise a mechanism the real server
# never offered. They are refused.
S: "SASL" "PLAIN"
S: "STARTTLS"
S: OK "ready"
C: STARTTLS
S64: T0sgImJlZ2luIFRMUyINCiJTQVNMIiAiUExBSU4iDQpPSyAiaW5qZWN0ZWQiDQo=
FAIL Malformed
